ile he  was basically experiencing a media  blackout back in 2015 and once again  it's this centrist moderate non-starter  ideology the Guardian Pat put out an  op-ed  a couple days ago saying that Harris has  a great centrist platform no no no  didn't we learn from 2016 and then the  hill published an op-ed by a democratic  consultant and lobbyist saying Clinton  lost in 2012 because she was moderate  and conservative voters supported Barack  Obama more okay the problem in 2016 was  partially that Hillary Clinton was to  the right of Barack Obama more centrist  and in part lots of other problems as  well they're going in the wrong  direction here I mean it's 2017 and the  Democratic Party is already setting  themselves up to lose the next  presidential election you know I think  because Trump is so scandal-ridden and  because the Republicans in Congress are  so ineffectual it gives this idea that  maybe you can just stay the course so  you don't have to go on the offense but  we've learned from 2016 that that's not  the case because Hillary Clinton  primarily ran an anti Trump campaign  correct she didn't promote any ideas of  economic populism that poll well for  broader Americans that could really get  you to the White House or just to win  majorities in Congress that's a path  that we have to take the center approach  basically means compromise right now  right center is for example when Barack  Obama starts negotiating Obamacare with  maybe a public option might be nice and  we get nothing except tens of millions  of new customers for private for-profit  insurance companies and I always like to  say this Obamacare did some good things  I've praised it for the good things it  did and I've criticized it for the bad  things that it did this will get us I  mean maybe I'm joking here president Ted  Nugent or something equivalent maybe  president Kid Rock who's running for  something up in Michigan I believe right  now this is the type of thing that will  get Trump r